    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "Validate the hypothesis regarding Ca/Si/Al/O glass conductivity by running a Molecular Dynamics (MD) simulation pipeline to compute ion mobility and conductivity as a function of Ca concentration, specifically testing the percolation threshold at 15 mol%. The workflow includes: (1) generating glass structures with varying Ca content (5-25 mol%) via melt-quench MD, (2) running NVT production runs to collect ion trajectories, (3) calculating mean squared displacement (MSD) and conductivity using the Einstein relation, and (4) analyzing the Ca-O-Ca network connectivity to identify percolation thresholds. This requires careful equilibration and convergence checks before property calculation."
    },
